Original commit body from f42d6880d8fdf43d55f0971aa70a4a90600f634a:

Three probes that re-priced the P1 queue existed only in a session
scratchpad on TMPFS, against the standing norm that measurement
instruments live in the repo. Each one is here because a claim it
tested turned out to be false.

measure-io-boundary-construct-ab.py answers every catalogue lookup
twice in one process — once as production asks, once with
call_construct withheld — so the filter can be A/B'd without a second
checkout. It is the tool that caught the construct-only form of the
rule removing 51 io-boundary matches on whisper.cpp, 49 of them true
positives, because call_construct=="method" means "spelled as a
selector expression" and Go spells os.Open(p) that way.

measure-taint-arm-census.py separates the section-3a confirm-only arm
from the WI-fasub barrier arm, which have different risk profiles: a
False on the second earns `sanitized` and deletes a finding. It prints
a caveat on a zero barrier count, because that arm is unreachable by
construction until the repo declares a sanitizer for the flow's label
— a zero there measures the catalogue, not the code. Merges the two
scratchpad variants behind a repo argument.

measure-call-construct-census.py counts the VALUE the F3 gate reads
rather than field presence. cpp carries the field on 41.1% of its call
edges and the one value the gate consults on 1 of 34,983.

Smoked on the merged tree. The construct A/B reproduces its recorded
numbers in both signs: 2 removals on whisper.cpp (sys/wait.wait,
kind=function) and 0 on nats-server over 27,755 method-construct
lookups with a module hint — the instrument fires, and the shipped
arity-keyed rule is non-destructive on Go.

